# The SGLang calibration member, on the cuda base: SGLang 0.5.20, the first release that serves
# this checkpoint (it registers Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration), and beside it harbor's
# distribution with the packages harbor imports and the packages the harness's roles import: the
# member starts each trajectory's sandbox itself. SGLang brings its own torch.
# Every package is named at one version and nothing is resolved: SGLang pins openai 2.6.1 and
# harbor's litellm needs openai 2.20 or later, so the set is no single resolution's; it is
# SGLang's own, then harbor's on top, which replaces that openai.
# cuda-tile 1.6.0rc5, which SGLang pins, is a wheel on NVIDIA's index alone, so it is named by its
# URL there. Compiled into member-sglang.txt by
#   hls images lock-pip layer member-sglang --task agentic_coding --server --no-deps
